          %p
            Overconvergent derived loop spaces are analogs of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+loop+spaces"} derived loop spaces
            adapted to the setting of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overconvergent+global+analytic+geometry"} overconvergent global analytic geometry
            = succeed "-modules." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
          %h2#overconvergent_de_rham_space Overconvergent de Rham space
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a global analytic space over a Banach ring
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+space"} de Rham space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi dR
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{dR}
            is usually defined as the quotient of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            by the formal groupoid obtained by formal completion of the groupoid of pairs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times X
            acting on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            along its unit section (given by the diagonal map). If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is separated, then this diagonal map is closed, and we may (in the affine case), see this formal completion as the spectrum of the projective limit of the quotients
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ℐ
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_{X\times X}/\mathcal{I}_{\Delta}^n
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times X
            around the diagonal. It may be an interesting question to try to relate sheaves on the corresponding quotient
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi X
                    %mi dR
                    %mo †
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\dagger_{dR}
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            by the corresponding groupoid to modules over the ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}^\infty
            of differential operators of infinite order.
          %h2#overconvergent_derived_loop_spaces Overconvergent derived loop spaces
          %p
            The basic idea of overconvergent derived loop spaces is to give a loop space version of the above construction of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mi dR
                      %mo †
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\dagger_{dR}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is an analytic Artin derived stack, we may define the associated formal loop space as the formal completion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{L} X
            of the loop space groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi LX
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi dSt
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LX=Hom_{dSt}(S^1,X)
            along the constant loop unit section
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi LX
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c:X\to LX,\;x\mapsto c_x
          %p
            Recall that more concretely, one will have
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi LX
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi X
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                      %mi h
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LX\cong X\times^h_{X\times X} X
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            inside
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times X
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                      %mi dagger
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^dagger_{X\times X}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mo †
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %mo †
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ×
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %mi h
                  %msubsup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %mo †
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  L^\dagger X=X^\dagger_{X\times X}\times^h_{X\times X} X^\dagger_{X\times X}.
          %p
            To get a sensible dagger generalization of the formal completion of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi dagger
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^dagger X
            along the constant loop unit section
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi LX
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c:X\to LX
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo †
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{L}^\dagger X
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mo †
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^\dagger X
            along
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi LX
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c:X\to LX
            %em Berkovich
            open subspaces of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mo †
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^\dagger X
            that contain
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c(X)
